{"authored" [{"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{16}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{16}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x & =3{sin}^{2}⁡x+3{cos}^{2}⁡x+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[3+\\frac{4}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(5+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})]-[5\\cdot 0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+1]-[0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi +4}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/5e40f35729a8e3df9f8403cad85bf0c4e6045733616c86cc399548a901c03ac7.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)+x-1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "c120718f931743c0d70fc46b9969277639e5f9861a4347dee3126eaccbdfe717" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab" "basis" 1134 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x & =5{sin}^{2}⁡x+5{cos}^{2}⁡x+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[5+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(8+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(8x+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[8(0)+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}(0)]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}(0)] \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-74401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (4-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x-\\frac{3}{2}(-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-74401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "4-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "4x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "4x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-114677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{16}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/ae150f223d210225b6490bebb859909b07842a8b7abb41137cf0206312aead2e.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-348705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (3{x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-114685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "3{x}^{2}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-114685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [3({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\pi^2}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x={cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cos}^{2}⁡4x-{sin}^{2}⁡4x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-74404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡2x-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡2x=2[\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡2x-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi +2\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2{\\pi }^{3}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi +\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3}] \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{8{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\pi +\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -7{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-7{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-49297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi (1+5{\\pi }^{2})}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi (3+7{\\pi }^{2})}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi (3-7{\\pi }^{2})}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi (7-{\\pi }^{2})}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi (3-7{\\pi }^{2})}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{sin}^{2}⁡x+11{cos}^{2}⁡x & =5{sin}^{2}⁡x+5{cos}^{2}⁡x+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+6{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5+6{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[5+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(8+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(8x+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[8(0)+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[4\\pi +\\frac{3}{2}(0)]-[0+\\frac{3}{2}(0)] \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361710" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x & =3{sin}^{2}⁡x+3{cos}^{2}⁡x+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[3+\\frac{4}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(5+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})]-[5\\cdot 0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+1]-[0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi +4}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/5e40f35729a8e3df9f8403cad85bf0c4e6045733616c86cc399548a901c03ac7.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)+x-1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi^2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/dcc78643dd44633f778d954de32a955dc5803abf7dc059c30bbbda97bc35413f.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. The area of the region is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x & ={cos}^{2}⁡x+({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }[\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi +3\\pi )-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\pi +\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-49294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "5\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{11\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/20844131c3d35b02f0ba7c6567b7765a54f0909e63ee309181dd5a25248dbfd5.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1=-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-2{sin}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-x+{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi -\\pi +{\\pi }^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{{2}^{2}}] \\\\  & =-\\pi +{\\pi }^{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}-4\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}+2\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3\\pi -2)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-49299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{\\pi }^{2}-1"] ["math" "\\frac{11{\\pi }^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi (3\\pi -2)}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi (8\\pi +1)}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-49299" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi (3\\pi -2)}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-51127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-51127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-51127" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-51127" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-51127" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-51127" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }[6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{4})-3+3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+x]\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{4})=3(1-cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,\\,[6{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{4})-3+3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+x]dx & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,\\,[3-3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3+3cos\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+x]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }x\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-348852" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348852" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi^2}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate\n$\\int 6{sin}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x$, we have\n\n$$\n2{sin}^{2}⁡3x=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{sin}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\cdot 2{sin}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 3(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-74411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x}{2}+C"] ["math" "3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "3x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C"] ["math" "x-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x}{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-74411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x}{2}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ so letting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}) & =1-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}) \\\\  & =1-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))={sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}(1-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}(1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2}x)\\,|}_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}] \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{\\pi }{3}]-[0-\\frac{\\pi }{6}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4"} {"question" "q-348837" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "q-348837" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\pi}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "b88e9b9bfe53daf9ad79f46b1a187aa4bdc2e7582f75781ec7861557ffc8bcf4"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab"}] "usage" {"q-74402" [] "q-361705" [] "q-348766" [] "e-483" [] "q-361710" [] "q-49297" [] "q-51127" [] "e-481" [] "q-348715" [] "e-484" [] "e-482" [] "q-10049" []} "basis" 1457 "retractions" [[17592186303641 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186097193 :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$∫_{π}^{2π}(2\\cos^{2} 2x - x^{2})dx$."] [17592186288705 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/5e40f35729a8e3df9f8403cad85bf0c4e6045733616c86cc399548a901c03ac7.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi